                    b: 'Correct — 44,100 Hz gives a Nyquist frequency of 22,050 Hz, just above the ~20 kHz upper limit of human hearing, so it captures all audible content without waste.',
                    c: 'The 44,100 figure is not derived from 440 Hz; that coincidence is not the reason.',
                    d: 'Backwards — HIGHER sample rates reduce aliasing risk; aliasing comes from sampling too SLOWLY.',
