                    a: 'Correct — the sources differ by 13 dB (>10 dB), so the quieter one adds less than 0.4 dB; the total is ~85.2 dB, dominated entirely by the louder source.',
                    b: 'Decibels never add arithmetically; 157 dB is meaningless here.',
                    c: 'Averaging the dB numbers is invalid; combining is an energy sum, not an average, and it lands near the LOUDER value, not between them.',
                    d: 'A +3 dB bump would require two roughly EQUAL sources; a source 13 dB quieter contributes almost nothing.',
