            judgeFraming: 'Judges probe standing waves because a project that "makes a tone" needs the student to explain WHY that pitch, not just that it happened. The distinguishing move is deriving the fundamental from the boundary conditions — nodes at fixed/closed ends, antinodes at open ends — and knowing that an open pipe gives all harmonics (fₙ = nv/2L) while a closed pipe gives only odd harmonics an octave lower (fₙ = nv/4L). A student who can point at an FFT and say "the even harmonics are missing because it is closed at one end" has demonstrated real command; one who just reads a frequency off a tuner has not.',
