                    b: 'Correct — the diaphragm and a fixed back-plate form a capacitor (C = εA/d). A polarizing voltage or electret holds the charge Q roughly fixed, so as the diaphragm moves and d changes, V = Q/C swings with the pressure.',
                    c: 'Piezoelectric (crystal) mics exist but are a distinct, third type; a condenser uses capacitance, not the piezo effect.',
