                    b: 'Correct — two equal, uncorrelated sources add in energy to give 10·log₁₀(2) ≈ 3 dB above either, so at equal signal and noise, half the measured energy is noise — a poor measurement.',
                    c: '6 dB corresponds to a fourfold energy increase, not the sum of two equal sources.',
