                    a: 'It is not exact at all amplitudes — at very high amplitudes the true equations are nonlinear and superposition fails (shocks form).',
                    b: 'Correct — linearity is an approximation valid when acoustic pressure is tiny versus atmospheric (~101 kPa); a loud 120 dB tone is only ~20 Pa, so ordinary sound is safely linear.',
                    c: 'They can interact — at high amplitude nonlinear effects couple them; superposition is only the linear-regime idealization.',
