                    b: 'Correct — modal density grows roughly as f², so bass modes are sparse and isolated (big peaks/dips), while high-frequency modes overlap into a smooth diffuse field.',
                    c: 'High frequencies do reflect; the difference is that many overlapping high modes average out, not that reflection stops.',
