                    b: 'Correct — inverse-square gives -6 dB per doubling of distance; 10→20→40 m is two doublings, so 68 - 12 = 56 dBA.',
                    c: 'Subtracting 6 dB per METER (or otherwise over-counting) is wrong; the rule is per doubling of distance, giving two steps here, not many.',
                    d: '-3 dB per doubling is the rule for a line source, not a point source; a point source loses 6 dB per doubling.',
