              judgeFraming: 'Judges ask "where does 0.161 come from?" precisely because reciting it proves nothing but deriving it proves everything. A student who can say "it is 55.26 divided by the speed of sound, so it drifts with temperature and becomes 0.049 in imperial units" shows they understand the equation is a packaged physical constant, not a magic number — and that awareness is what prevents the classic factor-of-3.3 units error that wrecks otherwise good projects.',
