                      b: 'Correct — the chamber computes α = A_sample/geometric area, and edge diffraction plus finite-sample/diffusion effects inflate the apparent absorption, so values slightly above 1.0 are an expected artifact meaning "extremely absorptive near the method’s reliability ceiling."',
