                      b: 'Correct — using only two reflecting surfaces means the least energy loss per cycle, so axial modes are the strongest and most lightly damped, and their fundamentals c/(2L) sit in the bass where gaps between modes are large.',
                      c: 'A rectangular room supports axial, tangential, AND oblique modes; axial are just the dominant subset at low frequencies.',
                      d: 'Axial modes are in fact the primary target of bass traps and placement; they are treatable, just stubborn because they are strong.',
