                      b: 'Correct — an absorber dissipates sound energy as heat (via porous flow or resonant loss), while a diffuser scatters a reflection over many directions and delays, preserving liveness while breaking up specular coloration.',
                      c: 'They are opposite strategies: removing energy versus redistributing it. Confusing them is the core error the lesson warns against.',
                      d: 'Both can be designed for various bands; the absorb-vs-diffuse distinction is about the fate of the energy, not a fixed frequency split.',
