                      b: 'Correct — coupled chambers open extra reverberant volume, lengthening and reshaping the decay (a shallower late slope), whereas curtains change the A term to make the room drier.',
                      c: 'They act on different Sabine terms (V vs A) and produce different decay shapes, so they are not the same.',
                      d: 'Neither is use-locked; curtains generally dry a room (good for speech) and chambers lengthen it (good for lush music), but that follows from their effect on RT, not a restriction.',
