              judgeFraming: 'Judges love this story because it is the field\'s origin myth AND a rigorous experiment a student can imitate: a vague complaint ("the room sounds bad") became a measured quantity (reverberation time) and then a predictive equation. If your project uses RT60, a judge will probe whether you know WHERE the number comes from — the right answer names Sabine, the seat-cushion decay experiments, and the inverse relationship RT60 = 0.161·V/A. Saying "I measured reverberation the way Sabine did, by timing a decay" signals you understand the empirical roots, not just a plugged-in formula.',
