              workedExample: 'Trace one listener\'s early reflections in each shape. In the Musikverein (~19 m wide), a side-wall reflection to a mid-hall seat travels only a few meters more than the direct sound, so the first lateral reflection arrives within ~15–25 ms — early and strong, cueing spaciousness. In a wide fan hall (~40 m at the rear), the nearest side wall may be 15+ m away and angled to send its reflection past the listener toward the back, so the first strong LATERAL reflection may be weak or effectively absent; the earliest reflections instead come from the ceiling (overhead, contributing little to spaciousness). In the Berlin Philharmonie vineyard, the listener sits against a terrace retaining wall only a couple of meters away, so that local wall delivers an early lateral reflection much like a shoebox side wall — which is precisely the trick that lets a center-stage hall feel intimate. The single variable that separates the three: how soon and how strong the first LATERAL reflection is.',
