                      b: 'The odd harmonics have antinodes (not nodes) at the midpoint, so they are strongly excited, not suppressed.',
                      c: 'The fundamental has its antinode at the midpoint and is in fact excited most strongly by a midpoint pluck.',
                      d: 'Pluck position strongly shapes the spectrum through the sin(nπd/L) factor — that is the whole point of the technique.',
