              judgeFraming: 'Judges probe pipe resonance because a wind-instrument project must explain WHY a given length produces a given pitch, not merely report a number off a tuner. The distinguishing move is deriving each fundamental from the boundary conditions — antinode at every open end, node at a closed end — and knowing the two formulas that fall out (open-open fₙ = nv/2L with all harmonics; closed-open fₙ = nv/4L, odd harmonics only, an octave lower). A student who can point at an FFT and say "the even harmonics are gone because one end is closed" has shown command; one who just reads a frequency has not.',
