                      b: 'Correct — a cylinder closed at one end resonates at odd multiples (f, 3f, 5f), so the clarinet overblows by a factor of three, a musical twelfth, and its even harmonics are weak.',
                      c: 'A fifth (1.5f) is not the resonance structure of a simple stopped cylinder; the odd-harmonic series gives a twelfth.',
