                    correctOrder: ['i1', 'i2', 'i3', 'i4'],
                    explanation: 'Inharmonicity puts the low string\'s 2nd partial sharp of a true octave; the tuner tunes to beats between that partial and the upper fundamental; killing the beats forces the upper note sharp of exact 2:1; accumulating this up the keyboard produces the stretched treble Railsback measured.',
