                      b: 'Correct — the corner circulates the string, and its round-trip time (set by L, T, and μ via f = (1/2L)√(T/μ)) fixes the period and thus the pitch, independent of the bow.',
                      c: 'β (bow-to-bridge distance) shapes timbre and the slip-to-period ratio, and it affects playability, but it does not set the fundamental frequency.',
                      d: 'Bow force sits inside the Schelleng playability wedge and affects timbre/clarity; it does not determine pitch.',
