                      b: 'Correct — the bending-wave speed (∝ √f) climbs from below the sound speed to above it, so there is always one frequency where it equals the trace speed of obliquely incident sound: the critical frequency.',
                      c: 'Damping affects the depth of the dip, not whether the wave speeds cross; the crossing is a consequence of dispersion.',
                      d: 'A panel\'s mass per unit area does not change with frequency; the frequency dependence is in the bending-wave SPEED, not the mass.',
