                      b: 'Correct — high damping limits the peak at resonance (valuable when spinning up through fn) but partially re-couples the mass to the floor above resonance, so steady-state isolation is worse than with a lightly damped mount.',
                      c: 'Color is irrelevant; this is about the transmissibility-versus-frequency behavior.',
