                      b: '45 dB far exceeds the ~20 dB practical ceiling of a thin barrier and is not what the Maekawa formula gives for N ≈ 2.',
                      c: '0 dB would require N near zero (line of sight open); here N ≈ 2 gives substantial attenuation.',
