                      b: 'Correct — Ctr weights low frequencies heavily to represent road traffic, and since walls transmit low frequencies most easily (and Rw under-weights them), the traffic-shaped correction bites harder.',
                      c: 'Impact noise is a separate rating family (Ln,w / IIC); C and Ctr are both airborne corrections.',
                      d: 'Ctr emphasizes LOW frequencies, not high; low frequencies are where partitions and the Rw fit are weakest.',
