                      b: 'Correct — when different samples read identically, sound is almost certainly bypassing them via flanking/leaks, so the rig ceiling, not the samples, sets the number.',
                      c: 'A broken mic would give obviously bad or noisy data across the board, not two plausibly-equal sample readings.',
