                      b: 'Correct — the reverberation-room (Sabine) method divides measured absorption by the sample\'s nominal flat area, but edge diffraction lets the panel absorb as if it were larger, producing apparent α values slightly above 1.0. It is a known, expected artifact.',
                      c: 'Values above 1.0 appear routinely in real ISO 354 / ASTM C423 data; they are not typos.',
                      d: 'Passive absorbers do not generate sound; the value is a measurement artifact, not emission.',
