                      b: 'Correct — τ_composite = 0.99×0.0001 + 0.01×1 ≈ 0.0101, so TL = 10·log10(1/0.0101) ≈ 20 dB; the 1% gap cuts the 40 dB wall to 20 dB, throwing away half the decibels.',
                      c: 'The loss is not linear in gap area; a 1% gap costs ~20 dB here, not 1 dB, because the gap\'s τ is enormous relative to the wall\'s.',
                      d: 'A 1% gap is devastating but not total; the composite is ~20 dB, not 0, since 99% of the area still has high TL.',
