                      b: 'Correct — a given phase error (say 18°) equals a fraction of a wavelength; since λ = c/f shrinks as f rises, that same phase error corresponds to a much smaller distance/timing tolerance at high frequency, so it is far harder to hold.',
                      c: 'Microphones handle high frequencies fine; the limit is the sub-millimetre positioning/timing precision required, not detection.',
