                      b: 'Correct — losing the transformer reintroduces most of the air-fluid mismatch, predicting a conductive loss of roughly 30 dB, matching clinical observation.',
                      c: 'It is a partial (conductive) loss of ~30 dB, not total deafness; loud sound and bone conduction still work.',
