              judgeFraming: 'Judges probe mechanotransduction to see whether a student understands that hearing\'s speed comes from DIRECT mechanical gating — a tip link physically pulling a channel open — rather than a chemical cascade. The sharpest signal is explaining why this makes the ear so fast (microseconds, no second messenger) compared with vision. Naming the tip-link proteins (cadherin-23, protocadherin-15) or the Hudspeth/Corey gating-spring model accurately, and honestly flagging that the MET-channel protein (TMC1) identity was long contested, marks a student engaging with real, still-evolving science.',
