                      b: 'Correct — Weber\'s law means the same 2 dB is easy against a loud standard and hard against a quiet one, so a DL is uninterpretable without the reference level (and better still, expressed as a Weber fraction).',
                      c: 'A ~1–2 dB change is near the typical intensity DL, i.e. right at the edge of detectability, not below all thresholds.',
