                      b: 'Correct — phase-locking, the substrate of temporal/periodicity coding, degrades above ~1.5–2 kHz and vanishes near 4–5 kHz, matching where musical pitch fades, which is strong evidence for temporal coding.',
                      c: 'The middle-ear (acoustic-reflex) muscles set loudness protection, not the pitch ceiling.',
