                      b: 'Correct — a mastoid vibrator shakes the skull and cochlear fluids without using the eardrum or ossicles, so it isolates cochlear/neural function from mechanical delivery.',
                      c: 'That describes an electrophysiological test (like the ABR), not bone-conduction audiometry, which is still an acoustic threshold measure.',
