                    explanation: 'Sound is captured by the microphone, the external processor filters it into bands and extracts the envelope of each, the coded stream crosses the skin via the radio-frequency link to the implanted receiver, and finally each electrode stimulates the nerve at its tonotopically matched cochlear location.',
