                      b: 'Correct — N = D²/(4λ) = D²f/(4v); it is the length of the collimated near field and the location of the unfocused transducer’s natural focus.',
                      c: 'Using D rather than D² gives the wrong scaling; the near-field length grows with the SQUARE of diameter.',
                      d: 'This grows with wavelength and would shrink at higher frequency, opposite to the real behaviour.',
