              judgeFraming: 'Judges probe transducer construction by asking why a matching layer must be a specific thickness AND a specific impedance, because a student who names only one condition has half the picture. The complete answer states both: impedance = geometric mean √(Z₁Z₂) so the two reflections have equal amplitude, and thickness = λ/4 so they are out of phase and cancel — the acoustic anti-reflection coating. Distinguishing the matching layer (crystal→tissue) from coupling gel (probe→skin air gap) from the backing block (damps ringing for a short pulse) shows the student understands three separate jobs, not one blurred "make it work" step. A student who conflates gel with the matching layer, or who thinks gel is a lubricant, reveals the gap.',
