                      b: 'Correct — magnetostrictive drivers are rugged, high-force, and efficient at low frequencies (cleaning ~20–40 kHz, welding) but eddy-current and hysteresis losses make them inefficient above roughly 100 kHz, so imaging stays with piezoelectrics.',
                      c: 'Bandwidth is not their selling point; they are typically narrowband CW power sources.',
