                    explanation: 'Harry Nyquist analyzed channel signaling rate at Bell Labs in 1928; Claude Shannon formalized the reconstruction theorem in 1949; digital audio samples at 44.1 kHz to exceed twice the ~20 kHz hearing limit; and pulsed-wave Doppler is the case where the sample rate (PRF) is capped by the speed of sound and depth via PRF_max = c/(2D), giving an unavoidable, medium-imposed velocity ceiling.',
