                      b: 'Correct — power Doppler maps the squared amplitude (energy) of the returning Doppler signal, so it is very sensitive to slow/low-volume flow, largely angle-independent, and immune to aliasing, at the price of losing velocity and direction.',
                      c: 'Peak velocity with a numeric readout is spectral Doppler, not power Doppler.',
