                      b: 'Correct — fₙ = (1/2π)√(k/m), so fₙ ∝ √k, and doubling k multiplies fₙ by √2 ≈ 1.41.',
                      c: 'Stiffening RAISES natural frequency; halving would require reducing k, or increasing mass.',
                      d: 'fₙ depends on both k and m through √(k/m); stiffness matters.',
