                      a: 'Correct — in the frequency domain integration is division by jω; as ω → 0 the divisor shrinks, so a tiny DC offset or near-DC noise is amplified without bound, appearing as a ramp or wandering baseline. A pre-integration high-pass filter is the fix.',
                      b: 'Integration attenuates high frequencies (÷ω), it does not multiply them; the drift problem is at the low end.',
                      c: 'Unit magnitude is a fixed scale factor, not a source of growing drift over time.',
